{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["ואשר לא צדה — like ״ואתה צודה את נפשי לקחתה״ — that he did not lie in wait to kill him." "אנה לידו — for he was liable to death at the hand of Heaven." "ושמתי לך מקום — once there would be cities for settlement. Because He had already said to them ״לא תרצח״ and also ״כבד את אביך,״ He therefore explained here their punishments. Also ״וגונב איש ומכרו״ — because He said ״לא תגנוב״ — and the Sages explained it as referring to kidnapping, a matter learned from its context, that it speaks of those liable to death by the court."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {2 "The Sages derive לא תגנוב (in the Decalogue) as kidnapping specifically from the parallel passage וגונב איש, since both deal with capital offenses; Rashbam cites this derivation concisely."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:24.019052522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}